# Line-ending policy, stated once and enforced here.
#
# The rule has three levels and they are NOT the same thing:
#
#   1. In the index (the blob) -- LF, always. `text=auto` normalizes whatever
#      lands in the working copy, so a Linux CI checkout and a Windows one
#      produce identical blobs and identical diffs.
#   2. In the working copy -- LF, except the two Windows-shell surfaces below.
#   3. In what we ship (dist artifacts, the zipfs image, the docs archive, the
#      release body and SHA256SUMS.txt) -- LF, no BOM, for everything we
#      generate ourselves. Vendor material keeps whatever upstream published
#      (see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and scripts/make-licenses.ps1, which copies
#      byte-verbatim and reports a vendor BOM instead of removing it).
#
# Nothing in this repository is binary today (123 tracked files: text,
# sources, license texts). If a binary ever arrives, it needs an explicit
# `-text` rule here, because `text=auto` guesses from content and a
# misdetected binary gets its byte pairs rewritten.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The single exception: cmd.exe reads .bat at its final resting place and
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads .ps1 the same way, so these check out CRLF.
# The blob stays LF, so cross-platform diffs of scripts are still clean.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Sources we author: pinned explicitly, so a future change to the default
# above cannot silently start rewriting them, and so `git check-attr` answers
# "why is this LF" without reading the default rule.
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.rc text eol=lf
*.tcl text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.editorconfig text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# Verbatim third-party license texts and the notices document: pinned to LF
# explicitly (redundant with the default today, kept so that a future change
# to the default cannot silently rewrite a vendor text). A checkout is
# therefore content-identical to upstream apart from line endings, which is
# exactly what scripts/make-licenses.ps1 -Check asserts -- EOL-insensitively,
# by design.
LICENSE text eol=lf
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md text eol=lf
LICENSES/** text eol=lf
